WEBVTT

00:10.190 --> 00:10.240
Natsume's Book of Friends 6

00:15.990 --> 00:19.990
Things I want are beyond my reach

00:19.990 --> 00:23.970
Wishes I pray for won't ever come true

00:23.970 --> 00:31.330
I hate myself for having these depressing and envious thoughts

00:31.840 --> 00:35.780
But I'm not alone in being like that

00:35.780 --> 00:39.780
And I believe that there's a bud

00:39.780 --> 00:47.310
That won't turn into a beautiful flower unless I make it bloom

00:49.030 --> 00:57.560
I'll accept all the regrets and worries that I've had until now

00:57.560 --> 00:59.600
And water the bud in my heart

00:59.600 --> 01:05.460
I'm sure there's a meaning to all the tears I've shed

01:05.460 --> 01:09.450
I've always been searching for what was born from them

01:09.450 --> 01:13.410
And realized it's always been right here

01:13.410 --> 01:17.420
If only I can love myself the way I am

01:17.420 --> 01:21.220
It'll become my own beautiful flower

01:21.220 --> 01:28.560
I won't hesitate anymore and make it bloom

01:32.820 --> 01:34.650
I'm so tired.

01:34.650 --> 01:37.280
Hey, Natsume, carry me.

01:37.280 --> 01:38.500
No way.

01:38.500 --> 01:40.070
It'll just make me hotter.

01:40.070 --> 01:41.700
What?!

01:41.700 --> 01:45.050
Don't you want to help me out?

01:45.050 --> 01:50.810
You were the one who started talking about Nanatsujiya sweet bean jellies, so we're going to get some.

02:00.690 --> 02:01.850
Are you okay?

02:03.460 --> 02:04.630
Ow...

02:04.630 --> 02:06.080
My hips.

02:06.080 --> 02:08.690
I'm sorry. Can you help me?

02:08.690 --> 02:09.840
Sure.

02:09.840 --> 02:10.730
Here.

02:12.030 --> 02:12.630
Huh?

02:14.070 --> 02:19.500
Young man, my home is nearby. Will you take me there?

02:19.500 --> 02:21.990
Huh? Okay, sure.

02:22.860 --> 02:24.550
Where is it?

02:24.550 --> 02:25.500
Over there.

02:27.500 --> 02:28.870
<i>It's far.</i>

02:28.870 --> 02:30.450
<i>That's the next town over.</i>

02:34.250 --> 02:38.260
The Stump of the Ringing Tree

02:44.290 --> 02:45.500
<i>He's light.</i>

02:45.500 --> 02:48.590
<i>Do elderly people's bodies get like this?</i>

02:48.590 --> 02:51.440
Hey, that's Natsume of the Book of Friends, right?

02:51.440 --> 02:54.900
Eek! We'd better run away before he calls our names!

02:58.090 --> 03:02.200
You've got something interesting, young one.

03:02.200 --> 03:04.030
<i>Oh no. Is he a demon?</i>

03:04.590 --> 03:07.410
You finally noticed? Idiot.

03:07.410 --> 03:10.980
Master, you need to point that stuff out.

03:10.980 --> 03:17.770
His aura is on the verge of getting snuffed out,
so I was waiting to see how long it'd take you to notice.

03:17.770 --> 03:21.240
We're almost there, young one.

03:21.240 --> 03:23.930
See that lantern up ahead?

03:24.330 --> 03:25.660
I live right next to it.

03:29.710 --> 03:32.550
I'm finally back.

03:32.550 --> 03:35.940
Sorry, young one, but could you could get me some water?

03:36.800 --> 03:38.440
This is your home?

03:38.980 --> 03:43.200
It's not where I live. It's who I am.

03:43.620 --> 03:45.580
<i>I remember hearing about this tree this morning.</i>

03:47.370 --> 03:50.080
The ringing tree's been cut down.

03:50.080 --> 03:51.860
The ringing tree?

03:51.860 --> 03:53.510
Yeah. Look.

03:54.080 --> 04:01.090
A shrine in the next town had a tree that was hundreds of years old,

03:54.080 --> 04:01.090
More Than
200 Year Old
"Ringing"
Gingko Tree
Cut Down
Today After
It Was
Damaged By
Lighting

04:01.090 --> 04:03.870
but it was struck by lightning the other day.

04:03.870 --> 04:05.270
Oh my.

04:07.180 --> 04:09.270
That was awful.

04:19.110 --> 04:22.350
Suddenly everything went white.

04:30.030 --> 04:30.790
What—

04:32.560 --> 04:37.000
I almost ended up as lumber.

04:45.780 --> 04:47.760
I feel revived.

04:47.760 --> 04:51.390
Hey, Natsume. How long are you going to stay here?

04:51.390 --> 04:53.730
The jelly will sell out.

04:53.730 --> 04:55.270
You're right.

04:56.270 --> 04:59.180
Okay, we're leaving.

04:59.180 --> 05:00.570
Wait.

05:00.570 --> 05:07.640
Natsume, is there one other thing you can for this old man?

05:07.640 --> 05:09.780
It'd better not be trouble.

05:09.780 --> 05:12.610
It's nothing that bad.

05:12.610 --> 05:17.290
I want you to bring water here for a few days.

05:17.290 --> 05:18.290
Huh?

05:18.290 --> 05:21.300
Not that long.

05:21.300 --> 05:25.220
This tree's life will end soon, as will mine.

05:25.840 --> 05:29.430
But there's one thing that needs to be done.

05:30.140 --> 05:33.430
I made a promise with a certain human.

05:35.010 --> 05:40.540
It's a very important promise,
and I cannot disappear without fulfilling it.

05:40.540 --> 05:41.720
What is it?

05:41.720 --> 05:43.690
Natsume, ignore him.

05:44.160 --> 05:45.700
It is...

05:46.510 --> 05:48.480
You see, it is...

05:49.950 --> 05:51.200
I forget.

05:51.200 --> 05:52.950
What?

05:53.460 --> 05:56.850
The lightning was a big shock, you see.

05:56.850 --> 06:03.710
But I remembered that there was a promise, so I used the last of my power to return.

06:05.210 --> 06:11.480
It feels like if I talk with you, a human,
then I'll be able to remember something.

06:11.480 --> 06:18.580
So bring water for a while, and if every day is
too much trouble, then you can skip rainy days.

06:21.650 --> 06:26.490
Shigeru, about the ringing tree that you were talking about this morning...

06:26.780 --> 06:30.320
It got an article in the paper,
so does that mean it was famous?

06:30.320 --> 06:31.600
Yes.

06:31.600 --> 06:36.420
We always saw it on our way to the shrine during festivals.

06:36.420 --> 06:39.670
It was a big and impressive tree.

06:39.670 --> 06:40.750
I see.

06:41.620 --> 06:45.500
Actually, I was going for a walk nearby, so I decided to go take a look.

06:45.900 --> 06:48.120
Oh? How'd it look?

06:48.120 --> 06:50.380
There was just a stump.

06:50.380 --> 06:52.070
I see.

06:52.070 --> 06:53.780
That's kind of sad.

06:53.780 --> 06:57.410
Why do they call it the ringing tree, Shigeru?

06:57.410 --> 06:59.020
I don't know.

06:59.460 --> 07:02.370
I think there was some kind of old legend.

07:05.070 --> 07:07.960
You made another stupid promise.

07:07.960 --> 07:11.210
You're the one who told me to care more for others.

07:11.210 --> 07:16.360
And despite what he said,
you don't know when he'll disappear.

07:16.360 --> 07:19.040
He may outlive you.

07:19.040 --> 07:20.040
He might?

07:20.340 --> 07:23.030
That's how the lives of trees work.

07:23.030 --> 07:26.690
They don't just disappear once they become a seedling.

07:26.690 --> 07:32.300
Of course, I don't know about a spirit given life by that tree.

07:32.800 --> 07:37.540
Master, I didn't make it just out of sympathy.

07:38.560 --> 07:45.060
Book of Friends

07:38.900 --> 07:42.840
He said it was a promise with a human, right?

07:42.840 --> 07:47.570
I want to know what kind of promise a human and a spirit can make.

07:48.180 --> 07:52.070
You're such a pain in the butt.

08:02.000 --> 08:05.020
Could the person you made the promise to see you as well?

08:05.020 --> 08:07.340
I couldn't say.

08:07.780 --> 08:12.960
Sometimes I seemed to be human.

08:12.960 --> 08:15.850
Mostly to young children, though.

08:16.740 --> 08:21.120
Have you ever heard of a person named Natsume Reiko?

08:21.780 --> 08:22.910
Reiko?

08:23.700 --> 08:25.600
I have not.

08:25.600 --> 08:30.030
Does she have something to do with the thing you're carrying?

08:32.140 --> 08:35.080
Seems I shouldn't have asked.

08:35.080 --> 08:38.620
You have your own reasons.

08:38.620 --> 08:40.120
I won't ask more.

08:40.430 --> 08:43.470
I'm tired, so I'll sleep for a while.

08:43.470 --> 08:45.390
Thanks for helping me today.

08:49.640 --> 08:53.880
<i>For a while after, I went to the stump every day.</i>

08:54.620 --> 08:57.930
<i>It felt like doing a part-time job.</i>

09:04.820 --> 09:07.900
Oh, so you got the same homework?

09:08.380 --> 09:12.710
We decided to go to Tanuma's place to do it.

09:12.710 --> 09:14.390
I'm in!

09:14.390 --> 09:15.280
How about you, Natsume?

09:15.740 --> 09:18.530
Sorry, but I have something to do.

09:18.530 --> 09:19.770
I see.

09:20.530 --> 09:21.610
Bye.

09:21.610 --> 09:22.260
Yeah.

09:22.260 --> 09:24.050
Bye, Natsume.

09:22.260 --> 09:24.050
See you later, Natsume.

09:27.900 --> 09:31.050
A way to get memories back, huh?

09:31.410 --> 09:37.600
If lightning did it, why not have him get struck by lightning again, and maybe he'll get better?

09:37.600 --> 09:39.680
Lightning! Blightning!

09:41.430 --> 09:42.840
No way.

09:42.840 --> 09:45.920
I'll look for a good medicine.

09:45.920 --> 09:47.520
Thanks, Hinoe.

09:47.520 --> 09:50.940
You could simply order us to water it.

09:51.220 --> 09:52.290
Yeah.

09:52.290 --> 09:54.690
On days I can't go, please do.

09:54.690 --> 09:56.690
Of course.

09:56.690 --> 09:59.510
You can just leave it to the Party of Dogs!

09:59.510 --> 10:01.140
You sure can!

10:01.140 --> 10:02.190
Thanks.

10:15.360 --> 10:18.380
Nobody ever comes this way, huh?

10:18.380 --> 10:23.320
They made a new trail to the shrine.

10:23.320 --> 10:23.720
See?

10:24.330 --> 10:27.980
It's close to the path traveled by something called a "bus."

10:27.980 --> 10:31.740
So that's the main trail now.

10:31.740 --> 10:35.730
They used to walk by here.

10:36.290 --> 10:41.240
I watched the people go up and back from above the trees.

10:41.660 --> 10:45.490
They looked so happy.

10:48.640 --> 10:50.100
Don't worry.

10:50.100 --> 10:53.500
The time is coming for me to
return to the ground, that's all.

10:53.840 --> 11:00.510
As long as I'm here, the other trees can't receive the power I must give them.

11:01.260 --> 11:03.870
I feel bad for them.

11:05.060 --> 11:08.070
Natsume's Book of Friends 6

11:08.850 --> 11:11.810
Oh, right. I found out where the name "ringing tree" came from.

11:11.810 --> 11:14.570
The ginkgo tree on the road to the shrine?

11:14.570 --> 11:19.120
Yeah, I got curious, so I asked a friend.

11:19.120 --> 11:30.330
It has that name because sometimes the rustling of the leaves made a sound like ringing bells.

11:30.330 --> 11:31.870
I see.

11:31.870 --> 11:36.090
But not everyone could hear it.

11:36.090 --> 11:39.920
Hey, it's almost time for the festival.

11:39.920 --> 11:45.020
It's a shame the tree's gone, but why don't we go see it?

11:45.020 --> 11:46.150
Sounds great.

11:46.150 --> 11:47.350
How about it, Takashi?

11:47.350 --> 11:49.830
I'd love to go.

11:54.720 --> 11:57.010
What are you looking at, Natsume?

11:57.010 --> 11:59.420
You don't have to go today, right?

11:59.420 --> 12:00.240
Yeah.

12:00.240 --> 12:03.990
With all this rain, he'll be fine for a day or two.

12:03.990 --> 12:06.030
Yeah, you're right.

12:09.250 --> 12:11.260
I'll go take a look, Master.

12:12.740 --> 12:14.250
Sheesh.

12:26.760 --> 12:29.470
My leaves sounded like bells?

12:29.470 --> 12:33.770
Oh, that was my specialty.

12:38.530 --> 12:47.530
When I had many leaves here, as I swung my staff,
all the leaves would ring at once.

12:47.910 --> 12:52.790
Especially during the festival, I'd swing it as hard as I could.

12:54.290 --> 12:58.340
I remember. That promise was...

12:58.340 --> 13:01.300
It was a child's hand.

13:01.300 --> 13:05.820
It was the last year the festival passed by here.

13:05.820 --> 13:07.160
Are you sure?

13:07.160 --> 13:14.340
I remember being sad thinking it was the last time.

13:14.340 --> 13:17.010
It was after that.

13:18.060 --> 13:20.860
I can't remember...

13:22.220 --> 13:23.890
The sun's setting.

13:23.890 --> 13:27.430
It's time for the children of men to go home, right?

13:27.430 --> 13:28.600
Yeah.

13:28.600 --> 13:30.030
See you tomorrow.

13:30.030 --> 13:33.580
Natsume, thanks for coming today.

13:35.890 --> 13:42.890
According to Shigeru, the festival passed by the ginkgo tree until 20 years ago.

13:43.520 --> 13:47.470
If they were a child then, they must be around 30 or so?

13:47.470 --> 13:53.900
You're not planning on finding them and asking what their promise was, right?

13:53.900 --> 13:57.170
It's been 20 years. They probably forgot.

13:57.170 --> 14:00.920
They won't remember a promise with a spirit.

14:02.800 --> 14:05.490
<i>Then the day of the festival came...</i>

14:25.680 --> 14:27.360
We're almost there.

14:27.360 --> 14:29.510
It's near the lamps.

14:29.800 --> 14:30.960
Yeah.

14:30.960 --> 14:35.130
No one uses this path anymore, huh?

14:36.310 --> 14:38.020
Is this it?

14:38.020 --> 14:40.400
Yeah, it must be this.

14:45.240 --> 14:46.950
What a shame...

14:46.950 --> 14:51.660
It feels like losing an old friend.

15:05.340 --> 15:07.450
<i>Yeah, definitely!</i>

15:09.250 --> 15:10.430
You remembered?

15:10.730 --> 15:12.880
It must be because of the festival.

15:12.880 --> 15:16.680
The events of that night have come back to me.

15:17.980 --> 15:24.060
The night of the festival, there was a single child who didn't go with the others and just stood alone on the path.

15:27.350 --> 15:28.570
God?

15:29.690 --> 15:32.780
It's been so long since a human could see me.

15:32.780 --> 15:34.630
That makes me happy.

15:35.740 --> 15:38.850
You smell good.

15:38.850 --> 15:39.460
Huh?

15:40.830 --> 15:43.620
Because we own a bakery, maybe?

15:43.620 --> 15:46.090
It's the shop in front of the station three stops from here.

15:46.380 --> 15:48.540
It's the best around here!

15:48.540 --> 15:52.610
I asked why she seemed so upset.

15:52.610 --> 15:55.770
I was supposed to come with Sacchan.

15:55.770 --> 15:57.860
But we got in a fight.

15:57.860 --> 16:03.930
Sacchan was the florist's daughter
from next door and her best friend.

16:03.930 --> 16:06.640
You could just make up.

16:06.640 --> 16:09.200
But I can't see her now.

16:09.200 --> 16:10.860
She's in the hospital.

16:10.860 --> 16:15.200
And she can't come to the festival because it'll spread.

16:15.200 --> 16:18.870
Please, God! Heal her!

16:20.370 --> 16:25.730
I'm not a god, so I can't do that.

16:25.730 --> 16:29.530
And I can't move from here.

16:29.530 --> 16:31.630
I know. In exchange...

16:39.620 --> 16:42.150
When she gets better, come here.

16:42.150 --> 16:48.150
I'll show you something more amazing, and I'm sure you two will make up.

16:49.990 --> 16:52.100
It's a promise.

16:52.100 --> 16:54.220
Yeah, definitely!

16:54.220 --> 16:55.330
I promise!

16:56.460 --> 16:57.630
What's this?

16:57.630 --> 16:59.910
You don't know about pinkie swearing?

17:00.280 --> 17:01.540
Pinkie swearing?

17:01.540 --> 17:02.440
Yep.

17:02.440 --> 17:05.460
It's a spell that makes promises come true.

17:08.170 --> 17:12.670
It was the only time I did this pinkie swear thing.

17:12.670 --> 17:15.330
And what happened to her?

17:17.090 --> 17:18.800
She was just a child.

17:19.130 --> 17:23.310
She probably thought it was a dream
after she went home and calmed down.

17:23.800 --> 17:28.040
I waited every day for her to come.

17:28.040 --> 17:30.990
Did her friend get better?

17:30.990 --> 17:33.510
Did something happen to her?

17:33.510 --> 17:37.570
I worried, but I couldn't leave this place.

17:38.140 --> 17:40.330
There was no way to check.

17:43.830 --> 17:48.250
Why are you searching for the girl he made the promise with?

17:53.240 --> 17:54.510
Excuse me.

17:54.510 --> 17:55.920
Yes?

17:55.920 --> 17:59.850
Is there a bakery around here?

17:59.850 --> 18:02.220
What? A bakery?

18:02.220 --> 18:04.010
Do you mean the one next door?

18:04.770 --> 18:07.600
They moved years ago, though.

18:07.600 --> 18:09.610
Huh? Next door?

18:09.610 --> 18:14.480
Did a girl live there 20 years ago?

18:14.480 --> 18:14.530
Notice of Closure

18:16.010 --> 18:20.240
I see. An elderly man you know made a promise.

18:20.520 --> 18:23.850
He says he just now remembered.

18:23.850 --> 18:26.750
He can't move, so I came in his stead.

18:27.630 --> 18:34.000
I got in a fight with Ai over something silly and was hospitalized before we could make up.

18:34.790 --> 18:37.470
In the end, I couldn't go to the festival.

18:37.470 --> 18:38.760
And then...

18:39.630 --> 18:41.010
she was gone.

18:41.340 --> 18:41.900
Huh?

18:42.540 --> 18:44.250
It was a car accident.

18:45.680 --> 18:53.400
He must've regretted saying he'd show her the leaves of the ginkgo tree sounding like bells.

18:54.150 --> 18:57.150
He made a promise he couldn't fulfill.

19:00.450 --> 19:04.540
But isn't the ringing tree gone anyway?

19:05.970 --> 19:07.370
I see.

19:07.370 --> 19:12.150
So she didn't forget the promise.

19:12.150 --> 19:13.190
Yes.

19:13.190 --> 19:16.530
Then there's no need to wait anymore.

19:17.330 --> 19:20.600
You promised to come until I remembered, right?

19:20.600 --> 19:23.550
You don't have to come tomorrow.

19:24.030 --> 19:27.150
I remembered because someone was here to talk to me.

19:27.150 --> 19:29.250
Thank you, Natsume.

19:33.310 --> 19:34.220
Oh my.

19:35.600 --> 19:39.080
This was the tree Ai wanted me to see, right?

19:40.440 --> 19:42.180
Oh, I know.

19:42.180 --> 19:44.320
I looked for it after I saw you yesterday.

19:48.730 --> 19:52.040
She made it to give to me.

19:52.040 --> 19:54.080
Her mother gave it to me instead.

20:00.160 --> 20:01.120
Ai...

20:01.590 --> 20:05.270
I'm sorry I couldn't keep our promise.

20:17.020 --> 20:19.520
Okay, I'll be going.

20:19.520 --> 20:21.990
Say hi to your elderly friend, okay?

20:21.990 --> 20:25.630
Thank him for remembering the past.

20:25.630 --> 20:26.410
I will.

20:44.090 --> 20:45.550
What is it?

21:36.230 --> 21:42.830
<i>The ginkgo tree spirit was cheerful for a while after that.</i>

21:43.630 --> 21:47.510
<i>I kept bringing him water, until one day...</i>

22:06.490 --> 22:12.630
While I was waiting for the dawn to come

22:12.630 --> 22:18.250
I softly closed my eyes in complete silence

22:18.250 --> 22:24.720
But instead of a new wind I wanted to feel across my skin

22:24.720 --> 22:30.620
A ray of light shined into my heart

22:30.620 --> 22:36.980
Goodnight, my beloved first star

22:36.980 --> 22:43.650
I've been waiting for your radiance

22:43.650 --> 22:49.260
I won't ask you to grant my wishes

22:49.260 --> 22:57.530
Knowing that you're watching over me is enough

22:58.640 --> 23:04.480
You don't need to answer, but I want you to listen

23:04.480 --> 23:10.840
It's not a farewell, but these are my last words

23:10.840 --> 23:23.590
In this town you disappeared from, I'll keep singing your lullaby

23:23.590 --> 23:34.680
The one that keeps flowers blooming in my dreams
